      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Graphdatenvisualisierung im Web\"\n",
        "author: \"Sara, Silvia, Adam\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "bibliography: references.bib\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Intro (Warum Soziale Netzwerke schwer zu zeichnen sind)\n",
        "Soziale Netzwerke bestehen aus tausenden bis Millionen von Verbindungen.  \n",
        "Je mehr Knoten und Kanten hinzukommen, desto schneller wird die Struktur unlesbar.\n",
        "\n",
        "Das Problem: **Daten haben keine räumliche Ordnung** – nur Beziehungen.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 2. Was ist Graphdatenvisualisierung?\n",
        "\n",
        "Ein Graph besteht aus:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Knoten** (z. B. Personen, Seiten)\n",
        "- **Kanten** (Beziehungen zwischen ihnen)\n",
        "\n",
        "Ziel der Visualisierung ist es, diese Struktur **räumlich sinnvoll anzuordnen**, sodass Muster sichtbar werden.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 3. Herausforderung (Wann wird ein Graph unlesbar?)\n",
        "Mit wachsender Größe entstehen Probleme:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Kanten überlagern sich\n",
        "- Cluster verschwinden\n",
        "- Orientierung geht verloren\n",
        "\n",
        "Ab einem gewissen Punkt entsteht ein sogenannter **Hairball-Effekt**.\n",
        "\n",
        "[hier Abbildung von Silvia hin]\n",
        "\n",
        "Im folgenden werden drei unterschiedliche Ansätze aufgezeigt:\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4a. Kleiner Datensatz\n",
        "## Der Datensatz\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"two-col\">\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"text\">\n",
        "\n",
        "### Les Misérables Graph\n",
        "\n",
        "Der Datensatz basiert auf den Beziehungen der Figuren aus dem Roman *Les Misérables*.\n",
        "\n",
        "Er besteht aus:\n",
        "\n",
        "- 77 Knoten (Charaktere)\n",
        "- 254 Kanten (Beziehungen)\n",
        "- ungerichteten Verbindungen\n",
        "\n",
        "Jeder Knoten steht für eine Figur, jede Kante für eine gemeinsame Szene oder Interaktion.\n",
        "\n",
        "Dieser Datensatz eignet sich besonders gut, weil er klein genug ist, um jeden Schritt eines Graph-Layouts sichtbar nachvollziehen zu können.\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"image\">\n",
        "  <img src=\"assets/data/les_miserables.jpg\" alt=\"Les Miserables Charaktere Graph\" />\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "## Schritt 1 – Die Rohdaten\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"text\">\n",
        "\n",
        "Noch bevor ein Algorithmus arbeitet, besteht ein Graph nur aus einer Liste von Knoten und Kanten.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Ein Graph besitzt zunächst keine Positionen\n",
        "\n",
        "Es existieren lediglich Beziehungen zwischen Elementen – keine räumliche Ordnung.\n",
        "\n",
        "↓\n",
        "\n",
        "Das bedeutet:\n",
        "- keine Koordinaten\n",
        "- keine Struktur im Raum\n",
        "- nur Verbindungsliste\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "### Visualisierung\n",
        "\n",
        "Rohdaten als ungeordnete Struktur\n",
        "\n",
        "<script src=\"https://d3js.org/d3.v7.min.js\"></script>\n",
        "\n",
        "<script>\n",
        "\n",
        "const width = 800;\n",
        "const height = 500;\n",
        "\n",
        "const svg = d3.select(\"#graph\")\n",
        "  .append(\"svg\")\n",
        "  .attr(\"viewBox\", [0, 0, 800, 500]);\n",
        "\n",
        "const tooltip = d3.select(\"#tooltip\");\n",
        "\n",
        "let showCharacters = false;\n",
        "\n",
        "const characterMap = {\n",
        "  \"Cosette\": \"assets/data/cosette.svg\",\n",
        "  \"Enjolras\": \"assets/data/enjolras.svg\",\n",
        "  \"Eponine\": \"assets/data/eponine.svg\",\n",
        "  \"Fantine\": \"assets/data/fantine.svg\",\n",
        "  \"Gavroche\": \"assets/data/gavroche.svg\",\n",
        "  \"Javert\": \"assets/data/javert.svg\",\n",
        "  \"Marius\": \"assets/data/marius.svg\",\n",
        "  \"Valjean\": \"assets/data/valjean.svg\"\n",
        "};\n",
        "\n",
        "fetch(\"assets/data/les_miserables.json\")\n",
        "  .then(r => r.json())\n",
        "  .then(data => {\n",
        "\n",
        "    const simulation = d3.forceSimulation(data.nodes)\n",
        "      .force(\"link\", d3.forceLink(data.links).id(d => d.name).distance(50))\n",
        "      .force(\"charge\", d3.forceManyBody().strength(-120))\n",
        "      .force(\"center\", d3.forceCenter(400, 250));\n",
        "\n",
        "    const link = svg.append(\"g\")\n",
        "      .selectAll(\"line\")\n",
        "      .data(data.links)\n",
        "      .enter()\n",
        "      .append(\"line\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"stroke\", \"#bbb\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"stroke-opacity\", 0.5);\n",
        "\n",
        "    const node = svg.append(\"g\")\n",
        "      .selectAll(\"g\")\n",
        "      .data(data.nodes)\n",
        "      .enter()\n",
        "      .append(\"g\")\n",
        "      .call(drag(simulation));\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Default: Kreise\n",
        "    let circles = node.append(\"circle\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"r\", 4)\n",
        "      .attr(\"fill\", \"#666\");\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Hover\n",
        "    node.on(\"mouseover\", (event, d) => {\n",
        "\n",
        "      const connected = new Set();\n",
        "      data.links.forEach(l => {\n",
        "        if (l.source.name === d.name) connected.add(l.target.name);\n",
        "        if (l.target.name === d.name) connected.add(l.source.name);\n",
        "      });\n",
        "\n",
        "      link.attr(\"stroke\", l =>\n",
        "        l.source.name === d.name || l.target.name === d.name\n",
        "          ? \"#ff6600\"\n",
        "          : \"#ccc\"\n",
        "      ).attr(\"stroke-opacity\", l =>\n",
        "        l.source.name === d.name || l.target.name === d.name\n",
        "          ? 0.9\n",
        "          : 0.2\n",
        "      );\n",
        "\n",
        "      tooltip\n",
        "        .style(\"display\", \"block\")\n",
        "        .html(\n",
        "          `<strong>${d.name}</strong><br>Connections: ${connected.size}`\n",
        "        );\n",
        "    });\n",
        "\n",
        "    node.on(\"mousemove\", (event) => {\n",
        "      tooltip\n",
        "        .style(\"left\", (event.pageX + 10) + \"px\")\n",
        "        .style(\"top\", (event.pageY + 10) + \"px\");\n",
        "    });\n",
        "\n",
        "    node.on(\"mouseout\", () => {\n",
        "      link.attr(\"stroke\", \"#bbb\").attr(\"stroke-opacity\", 0.5);\n",
        "      tooltip.style(\"display\", \"none\");\n",
        "    });\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Toggle Button\n",
        "    d3.select(\"#toggle\").on(\"click\", () => {\n",
        "\n",
        "      showCharacters = !showCharacters;\n",
        "\n",
        "      node.selectAll(\"*\").remove();\n",
        "\n",
        "      if (showCharacters) {\n",
        "\n",
        "        node.append(\"image\")\n",
        "          .attr(\"xlink:href\", d => characterMap[d.name])\n",
        "          .attr(\"width\", 16)\n",
        "          .attr(\"height\", 16)\n",
        "          .attr(\"x\", -8)\n",
        "          .attr(\"y\", -8)\n",
        "          .attr(\"onerror\", \"this.style.display='none'\");\n",
        "\n",
        "      } else {\n",
        "\n",
        "        node.append(\"circle\")\n",
        "          .attr(\"r\", 4)\n",
        "          .attr(\"fill\", \"#666\");\n",
        "      }\n",
        "    });\n",
        "\n",
        "    simulation.on(\"tick\", () => {\n",
        "\n",
        "      link\n",
        "        .attr(\"x1\", d => d.source.x)\n",
        "        .attr(\"y1\", d => d.source.y)\n",
        "        .attr(\"x2\", d => d.target.x)\n",
        "        .attr(\"y2\", d => d.target.y);\n",
        "\n",
        "      node.attr(\"transform\", d => `translate(${d.x},${d.y})`);\n",
        "    });\n",
        "\n",
        "  });\n",
        "\n",
        "// Drag helper\n",
        "function drag(simulation) {\n",
        "  return d3.drag()\n",
        "    .on(\"start\", (event, d) => {\n",
        "      if (!event.active) simulation.alphaTarget(0.3).restart();\n",
        "      d.fx = d.x;\n",
        "      d.fy = d.y;\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    .on(\"drag\", (event, d) => {\n",
        "      d.fx = event.x;\n",
        "      d.fy = event.y;\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    .on(\"end\", (event, d) => {\n",
        "      if (!event.active) simulation.alphaTarget(0);\n",
        "      d.fx = null;\n",
        "      d.fy = null;\n",
        "    });\n",
        "}\n",
        "</script>\n",
        "\n",
        "- ungeordnete Punkte  \n",
        "- oder einfache Node-Link-Liste  \n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "<details class=\"acc\">\n",
        "\n",
        "<summary>\n",
        "<span class=\"acc-toggle\"></span>\n",
        "<span class=\"acc-title\">Wie D3 einen Graphen intern speichert</span>\n",
        "<span class=\"acc-tag tag-impl\">Implementierung</span>\n",
        "</summary>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"acc-body\">\n",
        "\n",
        "### JSON-Struktur in D3\n",
        "\n",
        "Ein Graph wird typischerweise so gespeichert:\n",
        "\n",
        "```json\n",
        "{\n",
        "  \"nodes\": [\n",
        "    { \"id\": \"A\" },\n",
        "    { \"id\": \"B\" }\n",
        "  ],\n",
        "  \"links\": [\n",
        "    { \"source\": \"A\", \"target\": \"B\" }\n",
        "  ]\n",
        "}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "## Schritt 2 – Warum das nicht funktioniert\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"two-col\">\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"text\">\n",
        "\n",
        "Jetzt werden die gleichen Daten genommen, aber die Knoten zufällig im Raum verteilt.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Können wir daraus etwas erkennen?\n",
        "\n",
        "Eigentlich nicht.\n",
        "\n",
        "↓\n",
        "\n",
        "- Cluster fehlen  \n",
        "- Beziehungen sind unübersichtlich  \n",
        "- Positionen haben keine Bedeutung  \n",
        "\n",
        "Die Struktur ist zwar vollständig vorhanden, aber visuell verloren gegangen.\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"image\">\n",
        "\n",
        "### Zufällige Positionen\n",
        "\n",
        "<div id=\"graph-random\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "<details class=\"acc\">\n",
        "<summary>\n",
        "<span class=\"acc-toggle\"></span>\n",
        "<span class=\"acc-title\">Warum zufällige Koordinaten keine Information enthalten</span>\n",
        "<span class=\"acc-tag tag-konzept\">Konzept</span>\n",
        "</summary>\n",
        "\n",
        "<div class=\"acc-body\">\n",
        "\n",
        "Positionen sind willkürlich.\n",
        "\n",
        "Ein Graph definiert nur:\n",
        "\n",
        "- welche Knoten verbunden sind  \n",
        "\n",
        "nicht:\n",
        "\n",
        "- wo sie im Raum liegen  \n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "</details>\n",
        "\n",
        "<script src=\"https://d3js.org/d3.v7.min.js\"></script>\n",
        "\n",
        "<script>\n",
        "fetch(\"assets/data/les_miserables.json\")\n",
        "  .then(r => r.json())\n",
        "  .then(data => {\n",
        "\n",
        "    const width = 800;\n",
        "    const height = 500;\n",
        "\n",
        "    const svg = d3.select(\"#graph-random\")\n",
        "      .append(\"svg\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"viewBox\", [0, 0, width, height]);\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Links\n",
        "    svg.append(\"g\")\n",
        "      .selectAll(\"line\")\n",
        "      .data(data.links)\n",
        "      .enter()\n",
        "      .append(\"line\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"stroke\", \"#bbb\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"stroke-opacity\", 0.3);\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Nodes\n",
        "    svg.append(\"g\")\n",
        "      .selectAll(\"circle\")\n",
        "      .data(data.nodes)\n",
        "      .enter()\n",
        "      .append(\"circle\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"r\", 3)\n",
        "      .attr(\"fill\", \"#777\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"cx\", () => Math.random() * width)\n",
        "      .attr(\"cy\", () => Math.random() * height);\n",
        "\n",
        "    // Random edges (keine Struktur sichtbar)\n",
        "    svg.selectAll(\"line\")\n",
        "      .attr(\"x1\", () => Math.random() * width)\n",
        "      .attr(\"y1\", () => Math.random() * height)\n",
        "      .attr(\"x2\", () => Math.random() * width)\n",
        "      .attr(\"y2\", () => Math.random() * height);\n",
        "\n",
        "  });\n",
        "</script>\n",
        "\n",
